    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0406" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg344"/>

                <head>No. 204.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Edward Thornton to Mr.
                    Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-02-19"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 19, 1878</date>.
                        (Received February 20.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith, for
                    the information of your government, copy of a dispatch, and of its inclosures,
                    which I have received from the governor-general of Canada relative to the
                    supposed intention of “Sitting Bull” to enter the United States for hostile
                    purposes, and informing me of the precautions taken by the Canadian Government
                    in this matter.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDW’D THORNTON.</signed></closer>






